  "id": "Compound::DB01110 - Gene::3782",
  "verbalization": "Miconazole appears to interact with Kcnn3 through a shared pathway involving calcium-activated potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Miconazole binds to Kcnn1 or Kcnmb3, both of which participate in the activation of calcium-dependent potassium channels. These channels, in turn, are participated by Kcnn3, indicating a potential functional link between Miconazole and Kcnn3. The cumulative scores from the three paths support a mechanism where Miconazole modulates potassium channel activity, potentially influencing cellular signaling through Kcnn3. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Miconazole in regulating potassium channel function, which could have implications for its pharmacological effects.",
